   },
   "text": "Conserved Totals in a Four-State Enzyme Kinetics Model"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i1",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.45361,
    "y": 0.22284,
    "w": 0.09279,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "E. Kinetics"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i2",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.44393,
    "y": 0.25372,
    "w": 0.11215,
    "h": 0.01509
   },
   "text": "October 2026"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i3",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.46419,
    "y": 0.3066,
    "w": 0.07163,
    "h": 0.01258
   },
   "text": "Abstract"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i4",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.17398,
    "y": 0.3305,
    "w": 0.65206,
    "h": 0.05786
   },
   "text": "We track a single-substrate enzyme reaction through its four state variables: substrate S, complex C, free enzyme E and product P. Two totals are conserved along every trajectory - the enzyme total and the substrate total - and the product rises monotonically toward the initial substrate level."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i5",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.41474,
    "w": 0.27415,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "1 The reaction scheme"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i6",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.449,
    "w": 0.74117,
    "h": 0.01377
   },
   "text": "With association rate κ, dissociation rate λ and catalytic rate µ, the mass-action dynamics read"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i7",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.43192,
    "y": 0.47816,
    "w": 0.43867,
    "h": 0.01556
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { S } = - \\kappa S E + \\lambda C ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i8",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.41455,
    "y": 0.50911,
    "w": 0.45604,
    "h": 0.01556
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { C } = \\kappa S E - \\lambda C - \\mu C ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i9",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.40753,
    "y": 0.53439,
    "w": 0.46305,
    "h": 0.01556
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { E } = - \\kappa S E + \\lambda C + \\mu C ,"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i10",
   "kind": "formula",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.4668,
    "y": 0.55967,
    "w": 0.40379,
    "h": 0.01556
   },
   "latex": "\\dot { P } = \\mu C ."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i11",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.60138,
    "w": 0.28681,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "2 Initial state and rates"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i12",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.63564,
    "w": 0.74118,
    "h": 0.03088
   },
   "text": "The assay starts with substrate and enzyme only, at the recorded initial state S(0) = 1, C(0) = 0, E(0) = 0.1 and P(0) = 0. The nominal rates are κ = 1.0, λ = 0.2 and µ = 0.4."
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i13",
   "kind": "section_header",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.69267,
    "w": 0.15696,
    "h": 0.01811
   },
   "text": "3 Discussion"
  },
  {
   "id": "p1-i14",
   "kind": "text",
   "page": 1,
   "bbox": {
    "x": 0.12941,
    "y": 0.72693,
    "w": 0.74116,
    "h": 0.04799
   },
   "text": "Because the enzyme is either free or bound, the total E+C stays constant; similarly S+C+P never changes. The conservation of both totals is the internal check used for every reported trajectory."
  }
 ]
}